# Force LF line endings to prevent CRLF corruption
# during OneDrive sync (extra CR bytes truncate file content).
*.json eol=lf
*.tsv  eol=lf
*.yml  eol=lf
*.py   eol=lf

# dist/ is generated build output, so a three-way text merge of it is meaningless —
# when a local build and the dfbnb-patch-build bot both touch the same file, git
# used to throw dozens of conflicts (43 on 2026-08-24). The "ours" driver resolves
# those to the local copy instead. Rebuild dist/ after merging to pick up the
# bot's data; the tsv/ and src/ inputs it builds from still merge normally.
#
# NOTE: this only fires when BOTH sides changed the same file. If only the bot
# changed it, git still takes the bot's version untouched — nothing is lost.
#
# Requires a matching local config (per clone, not carried in this file):
#   git config merge.ours.driver true
dist/** merge=ours
